    <section>
        <h3>How to avoid a wrong application</h3>
        <p>Imagine you have passed Class 12 and see an NTPC vacancy. First check whether the post needs Class 12 or a degree. A similar exam name does not mean the entry rule is the same.</p>
        <p>Next, use the age date in that CEN. Then check category proof, skill tests and medical standards. A medical standard is the health requirement for a post. Do not assume all posts use the same standard.</p>
        <ul><li>Match the notice number on every page.</li><li>Read the post row and its footnotes.</li><li>Check education deadlines, not just course names.</li><li>Look for corrections on the issuing RRB website.</li><li>Use the application link given in the official notice.</li></ul>
        <p>This page helps you plan. It does not offer a job or submit a form for you. Keep your login details private, and save your application receipt.</p>
    </section>
